Dear Ms Zahmoul,

=20

Please find attached a judgment in this matter from His Lordship refusing p=
ermission to appeal.

=20

Kind regards

=20

=20

Karen

Karen Selby-King

Clerk to The Honourable Sir Jonathan Cohen

High Court Judge / Judge in charge of Family Division Appeals

=20

Clerk to The Honourable Mr Justice MacDonald

Deputy Head of International Family Justice for England & Wales

Family Presiding Judge for London

=20

*Also temporary Clerk to The Honourable Ms Justice Russell*

Phone: 0207 947 7426 Mobile: 07591 992371=20

=20

=20

=20

From: Nadia <nadia@rosekross.com>=20
Sent: 24 April 2024 20:10
To: Selby-King, Karen <Karen.Selby-King@justice.gov.uk>
Cc: Brent Molyneux KC <BMolyneux@29br.co.uk>; Nicholas Allen KC MCIArb <nal=
lenkc@29br.co.uk>
Subject: Zahmoul v Zahmoul=20
Importance: High

=20

=20

Dear Judge,

I need permission and court action to file the following:

=20
I seek to take court action against the Judgement made on 18 April 2024 and=
 I seek to file an application for a judicial review with the High Court.=20
I seek your permission to appeal the Judgement of 18 April 2024 as set out =
in my Appellant=E2=80=99s Notice FP161 form sent to you on 17 April 2024.
I seek to join Mr. Rakishev and Hogan Lovell to the civil proceedings. They=
 are necessary for a fair, independent, and impartial trial. I cannot have a=
 fair trial where the respondent is supported in the proceedings by =E2=80=9Cinvis=
ible=E2=80=9D parties, not when those parties order acts of violence against my ch=
ildren and me. My children=E2=80=99s lives and mine are in immediate danger, we ha=
ve been threatened several times and I have submitted the information and th=
e evidence to Your Lordship. I seek to join them to the proceedings in order=
 to have a fair, independent, and impartial trial.=20
I seek a Stay of the Proceedings until I have food and accommodation. It is=
 illegal to force me into a tradeoff of my absolute human rights under Artic=
les 2 and 6. It is illegal to fast track the Proceedings when I am hungry an=
d homeless as a result of the respondent=E2=80=99s breach of your order for MPS pa=
yments, as set out in my Appellant=E2=80=99s Notice FP161. The Human Rights Act of=
 1998 protects both rights, not one or the other.
=20

=20
Human Rights Articles 2 and 6
My human rights are protected by the Human Rights Act of 1998 as set out in=
 the European Convention on Human Rights. My absolute rights under Article 2=
 (the right to life) and Article 6 (the right to a fair trial) have been bre=
ached. My right to live and my right to a fair, independent, impartial trial=
 have been breached. The way the decision was reached is wrong and I seek to=
 cancel the judgement and demand compensation.=20

=20
Appellant=E2=80=99s Notice FP161
I sent Your Lordship my Appellant=E2=80=99s Notice FP161 on 23 April 2024 and I s=
eek your permission to appeal against the Judgement. I am not able to pay th=
e Court Fees due to lack of funds. I do not have any financial resources bec=
ause the respondent is in breach of the MPS order. I have informed the court=
 several times that the respondent is in breach of the order you made on 30 =
June 2023 paragraph 7.1 Maintenance Pending Suit. The respondent has failed =
to make the payments for March and April 2024. MPS payments must now include=
 rent as I have not been able to use the property in Wyoming since 1st Febru=
ary 2024 due to maintenance charges. Outstanding MPS payments of =C2=A351,524 (=C2=
=A318,762 per month in April and May, =C2=A37,000 per month for rent in February, =
March). I have no funds for food, accommodation, and basic necessities for t=
he children and myself. I don=E2=80=99t know the time limit to file my Appellant=E2=80=
=99s Notice FP161 and I don=E2=80=99t know the time limit to file my corrections to =
the Judgement. I am busy trying to protect my right to life and my right to =
a fair trial. The respondent=E2=80=99s breach with your MPS order means that I hav=
e to spend my time looking for money for food and accommodation, at the risk=
 of not having a fair trial. This tradeoff in my Absolute human rights betwe=
en Article 2 and Article 6 is illegal, unethical, and inhuman.=20

=20
Join Mr. Kenes Rakishev and Hogan Lovells to the Proceedings.
I seek to join Rakishev and Hogan Lovells to these Proceedings because they=
 are directly related to the threat to the children=E2=80=99s lives and mine. The =
respondent has tried to distance himself from Mr. Kenes Rakishev, Kazakhstan=
, Hogan Lovells, and the Accorda, but the links are well established and evi=
denced in documents filed in the Proceedings and in my emails to Your Lordsh=
ip on 7 March 2024 and on 9 April 2024. In particular, evidence sent to Your=
 Lordship on 9 April 2024 states that one of the parties=E2=80=99 minor children a=
nd I were involved in an incident on 24 March 2024 which is directly related=
 to the Proceedings, and which represents a direct threat to our lives. Furt=
hermore, evidence sent to Your Lordship on 9 April 2024 demonstrates that Mr=
. Kenes Rakishev and the respondent are business partners and explains why t=
his business association presents an immediate danger to the children=E2=80=99s li=
ves and mine. Rakishev is well known to the courts. He oversaw the restructu=
ring of BTA Bank following the bank=E2=80=99s collapse in 2009 and became Chairman=
 and CEO of BTA Bank in 2014. Mr. Hardman, partner at Hogan Lovells, oversee=
s Rakishev=E2=80=99s overall legal strategy and is known for his aggressive tactic=
s (see NZ1 attached). Rakishev is linked to Ramzan Kadyrov, Head of the Chec=
hen Republic, and designated by OFAC pursuant to the Russia Magnitsky Act =E2=80=
=9Cfor being responsible for extrajudicial killing, torture, or other gross vi=
olations of internationally recognized human rights=E2=80=9D. According to a U.S. =
lawsuit, =E2=80=9CKazakhstan v. Felix Sater=E2=80=9D, =E2=80=9CRakishev is reputed to have rap=
ed underage girls in Russia=E2=80=9D and organized =E2=80=9Cno holds barred=E2=80=9D fighting =
contests involving eight-year-old children. The defendant (Felix Sater) stat=
ed that he was =E2=80=9Cforced to hide in Israel for several months because Kenes =
Rakishev had, through Kadyrov, hired Chechen hit men to murder him=E2=80=9D. For t=
hese reasons, it is essential that Rakishev and Hogan Lovells be joined to t=
he Proceedings because I am attesting that they are providing significant le=
gal and financial support to the respondent, and I cannot have a fair trial =
if they remain in hiding. I seek transparency in the Proceedings above all a=
nd I seek to see in person those who threaten my children and me.

=20
Stay of the Proceedings and Confidentiality to Protect our Lives.
I seek a Stay of the Proceedings until I have food and accommodation, and u=
ntil I have free legal help and protection for the children and me. These ma=
tters are complex and involve a direct threat to my children=E2=80=99s lives and m=
ine. I seek a Stay of the Proceedings because without a stay, the Proceeding=
s and the Judgement would be unfair, inequitable and breach my human rights =
to life and to a fair trial. I am requesting that the information in this em=
ail remains confidential. I have copied Mr. Allen, Joint Head of 29 Bedford =
Row Chambers because Ms. Campbell has a professional conflict of interest as=
 she represents the respondent. Please note that Mr. Molyneux works at 29 Be=
dford Row Chambers as well. The email sent by Ms. Campbell in exhibit NZ2 in=
 which she copied the respondent represents an immediate threat to my safety=
 and that of the children.=20

=20

Sincerely,

Nadia Zahmoul

=20

=20

=20

=20

